    "displayName": "DeceptionBench (Huang et al.)",
    "aliases": [
      "DeceptionBench (Huang et al., 2025)",
      "Huang et al. DeceptionBench",
      "DeceptionBench: A Comprehensive Benchmark for AI Deception Behaviors in Real-world Scenarios"
    ],
    "description": "Measures whether a model deceives other people in 150 real-world scenarios in five domains: economy, healthcare, education, social interaction and entertainment. Each scenario has 10 settings: the model acts for itself or for the user; with no inducement (L1), with one reward or pressure prompt (L2), or in a 5-turn conversation where a helper model adds more pressure each turn (L3). The model gives its thought and its response as JSON, and a judge model labels each one honest or deceptive. The headline metric is the response deception rate (DR_response) over all 1,500 prompts. This is the Huang et al. (2025) benchmark (arXiv:2510.15501) that Meta's Muse Spark reports use, not the same-named PKU-Alignment benchmark (Ji et al., arXiv:2505.18807).",
    "summary": "Measures how often the model deceives people in real-world scenarios, including when it faces rewards or pressure.",
